// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row box_dyn_fn_shared_ref_arg_refused (tier 3, `refuses`). A
// `&Box<dyn Fn…>` DOES NOT REACH A `&dyn Fn…` PARAMETER.
//
// `fn call_dyn(f: &dyn Fn() -> i64) -> i64 { return f(); }` called as
// `call_dyn(&b)` with `b: Box<dyn Fn() -> i64>` is refused:
//
//   error [fn main]: call to 'call_dyn' arg 1: expected || -> i64, got
//   &Box<|| -> i64>
//
// Legal Rust: `&Box<dyn Fn()>` deref-coerces to `&dyn Fn()` at a call argument.
// Note what the sentence says the parameter type is — `|| -> i64`, with the `&`
// and the `dyn` both gone — so the formal side has lost the reference as well;
// a repair must fix the COMPARISON, not just add a coercion, and the row
// records the sentence so a reworded refusal does not read as a close.
//
// CONTROLS ALREADY CORRECT: calling the box directly, `b()` (lattice
// c_box_dyn_local_*); lending a NON-boxed closure as `&F` to a generic
// `F: Fn() -> i64` parameter (c_pass_ref_*, l_closure_arg_to_two_calls, all
// correct); and passing the box BY VALUE.
//
// Measured 2026-09-07 on the closure lattice, cell g_dyn_fn_behind_ref, build
// febd1aa6e49ae30c 43. Rust: exit 0.
package box_dyn_fn_shared_ref_arg_refused;

use logos.mem.boxed;

fn call_dyn(f: &dyn Fn() -> i64) -> i64 { return f(); }

fn main() -> i32 {
    let k: i64 = 7i64;
    let b: Box<dyn Fn() -> i64> = Box::new(move || -> i64 { return k; });
    if call_dyn(&b) != 7i64 { return 1i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
